  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef cv_rgb_to_grayscale(image: list) -> list:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **RGB to Grayscale** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef cv_rgb_to_grayscale(image: list) -> list:\n    arr = np.array(image, dtype=float)\n    return np.round(0.2989 * arr[:, :, 0] + 0.5870 * arr[:, :, 1] + 0.1140 * arr[:, :, 2], 4).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
